docs/input.md:18:## Keyboard movement
docs/input.md:20:- I05 - Give the board one remembered tab stop. When Tab enters the board, focus that card. Use the first card before any board focus has been remembered.
docs/input.md:26:| ArrowLeft | Previous card in the same row |
docs/input.md:27:| ArrowRight | Next card in the same row |
docs/input.md:28:| ArrowUp | Card in the previous row and same column |
docs/input.md:29:| ArrowDown | Card in the next row and same column |
docs/input.md:31:The board handles only these four arrow keys without modifiers, plus Enter and Space. It leaves every other key and modifier combination to the browser and doesn't use them to move focus or activate a card.
docs/input.md:33:- I07 - Stop arrow movement at a board edge. Moving left from the first column keeps focus on the same card.
docs/input.md:35:- I08 - Let native Tab and Shift+Tab leave the board. Moving through the board uses the movement keys instead of adding every card to the page's tab order.
docs/input.md:39:The board keeps focus separate from play:
docs/input.md:43:- I11 - On initial load, keep the browser's current focus. Loading the game doesn't move focus to the board.
docs/input.md:44:- I12 - After a new deal, Restart or a successful load, reset the board's remembered tab stop to its first card.
docs/input.md:45:- I13 - When a card receives focus, scroll it into view with nearest alignment in the board's scroll area. Give each card a scroll margin of at least 6px, so its complete focus outline stays in view, including mid-board cards.
